  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Conservation Actions for Golden-cheeked Warbler Winter Habitat PP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project objectives are: 1) To establish an updated and more accurate Golden-cheeked Warbler (GCWA) monitoring system in the pine-oak forests ecorregion of Central America, based on the analysis of historic and current data, in order to have more precise information about the proportion of the GCWA population that will be benefited from the management and conservation actions that the Alliance has been and/or will be implementing, 2) To increase the amount of GCWA.wintering habitat that will be under protection (10,000 hectares) or under sustainable management practices (10,825 hectares), thus contributing to the conservation goals of the Conservation Plan for the Central American Pine-Oak Forest Ecoregion and the Golden-cheeked Warbler, 3) To update the Conservation Plan for the next 5-10 years, linking information about new and current threats for the pine-oak forest and GCWA monitoring data</narrative>
  </description>
